From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn: EXPERIMENT keep the GPU unprobed for a sleep test

Diagnostic only. With the audio chain suspended and every other master
at zero in the AOP's low-power-mode monitor, the DDR-mode monitor still
shows the GPU DRV (and the AOP's own entry) holding a DDR vote for the
whole of s2idle; DDR stays at 1555 MHz and CX never collapses. Disable
the GPU node so the GMU is never initialised, and see whether the DDR
vote and the block go away with it.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi
@@ -826,7 +826,14 @@
 };
 
 &gpu {
-	status = "okay";
+	/*
+	 * EXPERIMENT (sleep investigation): with every other master idle the
+	 * AOP's DDR monitor still shows the GPU DRV holding a DDR vote through
+	 * s2idle, so DDR never collapses and CX never powers down. Keep the
+	 * GPU/GMU unprobed for one nap to confirm the GMU path is the holder.
+	 * Not for release: this leaves the device without 3D acceleration.
+	 */
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &gpu_zap_shader {
